      "text": "We start by observing the pattern of the given matrix product. The matrices given are all of the form $\\begin{pmatrix} 1 & d \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix}$ where $d$ starts from 1 and ends at 99. By performing matrix multiplication on these matrices layer by layer from the right, we can find a pattern and thus conclude the value of the resulting matrix.\n\n1. Multiply the matrix $\\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix}$ by $\\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix}$,\n   \\[\n   \\begin{pmatrix}\n   1 \\cdot 1 + 1 \\cdot 0 & 1 \\cdot 3 + 1 \\cdot 1 \\\\\n   0 \\cdot 1 + 1 \\cdot 0 & 0 \\cdot 3 + 1 \\cdot 1\n   \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix}.\n   \\]\n2. Multiply the resulting matrix $\\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix}$ by $\\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix}$,\n   \\[\n   \\begin{pmatrix}\n   1 \\cdot 1 + 4 \\cdot 0 & 1 \\cdot 5 + 4 \\cdot 1 \\\\\n   0 \\cdot 1 + 1 \\cdot 0 & 0 \\cdot 5 + 1 \\cdot 1\n   \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix}.\n   \\]\n3. Continue this process for each consecutive multiplication, adding an extra 4 to the resulting value for each $d + 1$ terms added to the right of the matrix as per the pattern observed.\n\nTherefore, after multiplying the matrix for every number $d$ from 1 to 99, our final result is the matrix,\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix}\n1 & \\sum_{d=1}^{99} d \\\\\n0 & 1\n\\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\nwhere the sum $\\sum_{d=1}^{99} d = \\frac{d(d+1)}{2}$. Calculating for $d=99$,\n\\[\n\\sum_{d=1}^{99} d = \\frac{99 \\cdot 100}{2} = 4950.\n\\]\n\nThus, our final answer is $\\boxed{\\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 4950 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix}}$.",
